content.text:
Yes — two things need to flip back when you're ready to go live:

**1. `appsettings.json`** — comment out `"Local"` and uncomment whichever live server(s) you want active:
```json
"server_ip_list": {
    ...
    "Com": "103.211.202.235",
    //"Local": "SERVER\\SQLEXPRESS"
}
```

**2. `Program.cs`** — swap the connection string back to the live one (`ADMIN_IMPEX`/`rtsadmin`), since that's currently commented out in favor of the local one we just enabled:
```csharp
string connString = $"Server={serverIp};database=ADMIN_IMPEX;uid=rtsadmin;pwd=adminrts@#12345@#rtsadmin;TrustServerCertificate=True;";
//string connString = $"Server={serverIp};database=ImpexLogin;uid=sa;pwd=SA,123;TrustServerCertificate=True;";
```

Both are manual, matching how IRN itself is set up — there's no auto-detection of "am I local or live," you just comment/uncomment the right lines in both files together before switching.

Want me to make that swap now, or are you not ready to go live yet (still testing locally)?

